A||||4||Fiero SE||How do I get the speakers out of the seat?||||5||
Z||000000||Fiero SE||12-20-1999||12:35 PM||||I want to replace the speakers in the seats and don't see how I'm supposed to get them out. And also, what size are the speakers in the seats? And what size are the speakers under the dash & and where can I get some? Thanks,  <A HREF="mailto:Alex985@aol.com">Alex985@aol.com</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||12-20-1999||12:45 PM||||There's a link for getting the speakers out of the headrests on batboys page.  (Go to his "secrets" page.)  I think you have to remove the seatback cover, but I could be wrong.  The size of those speakers are 3.5".  The only speaker I know of that is *under* the dash is the sub.  If you have a sub under the dash (it's 5.25") and seats with headrest speakers, someone has switched something in your car.  What year is your car?  The headrest speaker seats only came in '84 and '85s and the subs only came in '87 and '88 (maybe '86s, I'm not sure).  If you're talking about the speakers on your dash up by the windshield, those are 4 x 10s.  You can get those almost anywhere.  Radio Shack sell them for $14 if you really want to go cheap (I don't like the sound quality).  I just bought some good ones at Circuit City for about $80 (good, name brand, high powered speakers).  Hope I answered your questions. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero SE||12-20-1999||01:10 PM||||My car is an 84 SE and it has the speakers in the headrest. But under the dash they look like they have been taken out. That's why I was asking the size. Thanks for the help though. I'm going to see if my dad buys me the 86 or 87 (dunno what year)Fiero GT that is for sale though, it's a fastback. But I'm going to replace the speakers. THanks again.||||reg||10
Z||000003||BENGAL4||12-20-1999||01:33 PM||||Fiero SE,<P>I havent replaced seat speakers but I recovered my seats. It was real easy. Just unbolt the recline mechanisim and the bolt from the other side and the seat back is off. Unzip the bottom and roll it back about 3". On the front, you will see 2 rod's, one on each side. Cut the hog rings and pull the rods out. You will see hog rings as you go along, just remove them and roll the seat cover inside out. When you are installing the cover, just remember where you need to put the rings.<P>Good luck||||reg||10
Z||000004||DJRice||12-21-1999||08:40 AM||||If you mean the speakers in the dash then those are 4x10s.  You have two panels on the top of your dashboard that you can pry up carefully using a butterknife or something wide so as not to crack them.  If there are holes under there, then the speakers are missing.||||reg||1
